The graph of $y = \tan(3x)$ is shown for $0 \le x < \pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
  xmin=-0.2, xmax=3.5, ymin=-4.5, ymax=4.5,
  xtick={0.5236, 1.0472, 1.5708, 2.0944, 2.6180, 3.1416},
  xticklabels={$\frac{\pi}{6}$, $\frac{\pi}{3}$, $\frac{\pi}{2}$, $\frac{2\pi}{3}$, $\frac{5\pi}{6}$, $\pi$},
  ytick={-4, -2, 2, 4},
  samples=100, clip=false,
  restrict y to domain=-4.5:4.5, unbounded coords=jump,
  axis line style={-{Stealth}}, width=12cm, height=6.5cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=0:0.4419] {tan(deg(3*x))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=0.6053:1.4891] {tan(deg(3*x))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=1.6525:2.5363] {tan(deg(3*x))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=2.6997:3.1416] {tan(deg(3*x))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What are the equations of the vertical asymptotes in $0 \le x < \pi$?
